#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0192 expect=noViolation domain=PC
#note "SENDIG 3.1.1 section 6.3.13.2 (PC PP Cross-domain Example 2), the identifying columns of all 26 rows: PCDTC is null throughout and the Day 1 and Day 14 profiles repeat the same PCELTM values. Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner: key coalesce(PCDTC, concat(PCTPTREF, \"/\", PCELTM))): the observation time falls back to the planned reference + elapsed time, so the conforming example reports nothing. Red under the old PCDTC-only key (every record of a test shares the null PCDTC) and under coalesce(PCDTC, PCELTM) (Day 1 / Day 14 collide)."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset PC class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PCSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PCTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col PCSPEC   type=Char label="Specimen Material Type"
col PCDTC    type=Char label="Date/Time of Specimen Collection"
col PCELTM   type=Char label="Planned Elapsed Time from Time Point Ref"
col PCTPTREF type=Char label="Time Point Reference"
---
